/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (What this means is during an uptrend where price is making higher highs and higher lows, the price may break below the most recent higher low to grab liquidity then trade back in the direction of the original trend. This initial move lower to the untrained eye may cause traders to look for shorts at the next opportunity under the assumption the uptrend has reversed after the formation of the lower low but end up getting stopped out. The opposite can be said in downtrends.)
/E (What this means is during an uptrend where price is making higher highs and higher lows, the price may break below the most recent higher low to grab liquidity then trade back in the direction of the original trend. This initial move lower to the untrained eye may cause traders to look for shorts at the next opportunity under the assumption the uptrend has reversed after the formation of the lower low but end up getting stopped out. The opposite can be said in downtrends.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
