/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Firstly what is a break of structure? A break of structure in an uptrend occurs when price moves higher from a higher low to take out the most recent high. What this indicates is the trend is strong and likely to continue to the upside making the low a strong low.)
/E (Firstly what is a break of structure? A break of structure in an uptrend occurs when price moves higher from a higher low to take out the most recent high. What this indicates is the trend is strong and likely to continue to the upside making the low a strong low.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
541 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (A break of structure in a downtrend is a price move from a lower high that trades down to take out the most recent lower low to form new lows. This indicates a strong downtrend and likely continuation of the trend to the downside making the high a strong high.)
/E (A break of structure in a downtrend is a price move from a lower high that trades down to take out the most recent lower low to form new lows. This indicates a strong downtrend and likely continuation of the trend to the downside making the high a strong high.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
